Grammar G3 (page 39) is

P -> E
E -> E + T
E -> T
T -> ident
T -> int

So, we have

E -> E (+ T) | T
E -> E alpha_1 | beta_1

The substitution is

E -> beta_1 E' (because we only have one recursive rule?)
E' -> alpha_1 E' | epsilon

E -> beta_1 E':
E -> T E'

E' -> alpha_1 E':
E' -> + T E'

So our grammar becomes (G6):

P -> E
E -> T E'
E' -> + T E'
E' -> epsilon
T -> ident
T -> int
